00:56:16.680 --> 00:56:18.803
platform that we can use
for some of the metrics

00:56:18.803 --> 00:56:20.970
we're creating and some of
the analyzes we're doing,

00:56:20.970 --> 00:56:23.960
but that we're not going to
expose an endpoint to everyone

00:56:23.960 --> 00:56:24.460
else.

00:56:24.460 --> 00:56:28.050
So I think absolutely
the end state

00:56:28.050 --> 00:56:33.810
would love a world in which
people are pushing and pulling

00:56:33.810 --> 00:56:38.062
from our GitHub and saying like,
we want to add this new data

00:56:38.062 --> 00:56:40.020
set, and we're like, OK,
here's the conventions

00:56:40.020 --> 00:56:40.770
for the data set.

00:56:40.770 --> 00:56:43.080
If you put it in
this format, then we

00:56:43.080 --> 00:56:45.525
can add it to the
community data platform,

00:56:45.525 --> 00:56:47.010
but we're just not there yet.

00:56:50.360 --> 00:56:50.860
Thank you.

00:56:50.860 --> 00:56:52.900
So one more Slido
question and it

00:56:52.900 --> 00:56:55.960
was, what advice do you
have for someone who's

00:56:55.960 --> 00:56:59.090
interested in starting their
own data science consulting

00:56:59.090 --> 00:56:59.590
company?

00:57:02.775 --> 00:57:04.900
So I've known some people
who've gone that route,

00:57:04.900 --> 00:57:08.230
and it can be very rewarding.

00:57:08.230 --> 00:57:12.797
I will say almost all of them
will also tell you though

00:57:12.797 --> 00:57:14.880
that they were able to do
it for a couple of years

00:57:14.880 --> 00:57:16.088
and they got burnt out on it.

00:57:16.088 --> 00:57:20.460
And the main thing
is acquisition,

00:57:20.460 --> 00:57:24.310
customer acquisition
takes a lot of time.

00:57:24.310 --> 00:57:27.090
So I mean, just
pitching projects--

00:57:27.090 --> 00:57:28.500
And you don't
realize when you're

00:57:28.500 --> 00:57:30.090
working for a
consultancy, someone else

00:57:30.090 --> 00:57:30.923
does all that stuff.

00:57:30.923 --> 00:57:34.860
Someone else goes and finds
all the contracts and says--

00:57:34.860 --> 00:57:37.620
you're only seeing 10%
of the contracts that

00:57:37.620 --> 00:57:41.590
actually got pitched and signed
and executed and came to you.

00:57:41.590 --> 00:57:44.790
Whereas if you're owning
your own consultancy,

00:57:44.790 --> 00:57:47.370
you're the one who's got
to market and reach out

00:57:47.370 --> 00:57:49.950
to all these things and pitch
30 different things hoping

00:57:49.950 --> 00:57:52.620
two of them bite.

00:57:52.620 --> 00:57:59.620
So I would just say be prepared
for that part of the slog.

00:57:59.620 --> 00:58:04.980
But the advantage is you
have your own company.

00:58:04.980 --> 00:58:06.360
You get to work for yourself.

00:58:06.360 --> 00:58:08.500
Yeah.

00:58:08.500 --> 00:58:09.400
OK, maybe on a--

00:58:09.400 --> 00:58:11.260
Project you want.

00:58:11.260 --> 00:58:14.200
Maybe on a related note,
one last question for you

00:58:14.200 --> 00:58:18.160
because I realize it's already
the end of our time here.

00:58:18.160 --> 00:58:23.070
What is one of your favorite
pieces of career advice

00:58:23.070 --> 00:58:25.545
that you've ever
received or have given?

00:58:29.660 --> 00:58:32.120
Wow.

00:58:32.120 --> 00:58:33.110
Just so many.

00:58:33.110 --> 00:58:35.390
It's hard to narrow
it down to one.

00:58:35.390 --> 00:58:36.720
But if I--

00:58:36.720 --> 00:58:41.630
I think the biggest
one is when you're--

00:58:41.630 --> 00:58:44.990
remember that the interview
isn't just for the employer.

00:58:44.990 --> 00:58:47.570
The interview is for you too.

00:58:47.570 --> 00:58:48.830
Ask those questions.

00:58:48.830 --> 00:58:50.750
Don't be afraid to dig deep.

00:58:50.750 --> 00:58:52.760
Don't be afraid to ask to--

00:58:52.760 --> 00:58:55.820
can I talk to somebody who's
on the team I'll be working on?

00:58:55.820 --> 00:58:58.725
And not just my manager, like
somebody who's at my level.

00:58:58.725 --> 00:59:00.350
Somebody who would
be my peer because I

00:59:00.350 --> 00:59:03.290
want to hear from them.

00:59:03.290 --> 00:59:09.706
And just really make
sure that it's somewhere

00:59:09.706 --> 00:59:13.200
that you want to work.

00:59:13.200 --> 00:59:14.310
Absolutely.

00:59:14.310 --> 00:59:15.930
Thank you so much.

00:59:15.930 --> 00:59:19.760
Thank you, Nick, for sharing
your experience and insights

00:59:19.760 --> 00:59:22.020
with all of us and
taking the time

00:59:22.020 --> 00:59:23.340
to answer all of our questions.

00:59:23.340 --> 00:59:25.690
We really appreciate it.

00:59:25.690 --> 00:59:26.780
Yeah, I really enjoyed it.

